---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactBanner from '../components/ContactBanner.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Services — Raashid Arquil" description="Websites, focused web apps, and first-version mobile apps for small businesses and people with an idea. Start with the problem."><div class="shell">
<header class="page-intro compact-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Work with me</p><h1 class="display">Let's build<br/><em class="serif">what you need.</em></h1><p class="lead">Tell me what's difficult right now. We'll work out what would actually help, agree on a first piece of work that's worth doing, and build that properly.</p></header>
<section class="offer-list" aria-label="Services"><h2 class="sr-only">Services available</h2>
<article class="offer"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Websites</p><div><h3>A website for your business or product.</h3><p class="offer-who">For a small business, or someone launching something, who needs a clear site people can find, trust, and get in touch through.</p><p>A business website, landing page, or portfolio. Coded by hand, or built in WordPress and Elementor if you'd like to edit it yourself afterwards.</p><ul><li>The pages you need, agreed up front, working well on phones.</li><li>Built from your content and brand, with help spotting what's missing.</li><li>Put online and handed over, so you know how to look after it.</li></ul><div class="offer-proof"><a class="text-link" href="/contact/?topic=website">Talk about a website →</a></div></div></article>
<article class="offer"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Web applications</p><div><h3>One workflow, built properly.</h3><p class="offer-who">For a team still running something on phone calls, notebooks, or a spreadsheet that's outgrown itself.</p><p>SmartDrive started that way: getting my licence meant bookings by phone, records in a book, and queues with no order. A dashboard, a booking flow, or one focused feature, starting with who uses it and what they need to get done.</p><ul><li>One clear flow, and the screens it needs.</li><li>We decide together what it connects to, and what it doesn't need to.</li><li>Working versions to try along the way, not just at the end.</li></ul><div class="offer-proof"><a class="text-link" href="https://raashidarq.github.io/smartdrive/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Try the SmartDrive demo ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/work/smartdrive/">How I built it →</a></div></div></article>
<article class="offer"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Mobile prototypes</p><div><h3>A first version you can try.</h3><p class="offer-who">For someone with an app idea who wants something real in their hand to test with people, before committing to the whole thing.</p><p>An Android (Kotlin) or Flutter app built around one journey that matters, or a single feature for an app you already have.</p><ul><li>One journey done well, rather than a whole app done halfway.</li><li>Something you can install and try on your own phone.</li><li>An honest line between "first version" and "ready for the Play Store".</li></ul><div class="offer-proof"><a class="text-link" href="/work/cropcare/">CropCare: Flutter + on-device ML →</a><a class="text-link" href="/work/keepclose/">KeepClose: Kotlin, offline Android →</a></div></div></article>
</section>
<section class="section"><p class="eyebrow mb-4">How we'll work</p><h2 class="section-title">No surprises,<br/>start to finish.</h2><div class="process-grid">{[{title:'Understand',text:'We talk about the problem, who it’s for, what already exists, and your timing and budget.'},{title:'Agree',text:'We agree what gets built, when you’ll see it, and who does what. If something new comes up, we talk about it before it changes the plan.'},{title:'Build & review',text:'You see working progress at each milestone, so nothing is a surprise at the end.'},{title:'Hand over',text:'It goes live, you get access and a short guide, and we agree on any support after.'}].map((step,i)=><article><span class="eyebrow">0{i+1}</span><h3>{step.title}</h3><p>{step.text}</p></article>)}</div><p class="small-copy mt-8">I'm early in my freelance work, so I take on a small number of projects at a time and give each one proper attention. Every project starts with a conversation about the problem, not a quote.</p></section><ContactBanner/>
</div></BaseLayout>
